<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barrier Treaty (1715)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1715">1715</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Third Barrier Treaty · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Barrier Treaty of 15 November 1715, signed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> with British mediation, settled the status of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-netherlands">Southern Netherlands</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>. Austria took over the former Spanish provinces but allowed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> to garrison a line of fortresses, including Namur, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tournai">Tournai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ypres">Ypres</a>, as a barrier against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and paid towards their upkeep.</p></div>
